This project adapts parts of claude-subscription-directsdk, a plugin in
NousResearch/hermes-official-plugins (https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-official-plugins),
used under the MIT License.

Adapted parts:

- claude_code_bg/usage.py: the `/usage` plan-limits fetch through Claude Code's own
  `get_usage` control request (from `directsdk_setup.fetch_usage`) and the conversion of
  the plan-limits body into usage windows and detail lines (from `usage_windows`, with
  `LIMIT_LABELS`, `LEGACY_WINDOWS`, `_percent` and `_reset_at`).
- claude_code_bg/__init__.py: `classify_api_error` (the client's cancel error classified as
  a timeout, passed as a dataclass field of the profile), the `fetch_account_usage` and
  `get_usage_cost` pattern (an `AccountUsageSnapshot` from `get_usage`; a `CostResult`
  list-price estimate), and the provider profile layout (`auth_type='external_process'`,
  a `process://` base URL, `process_command` with `process_command_env_vars`, no `env_vars`).
- claude_code_bg/client.py: the `Client` outline (the `HERMES_SKIP_TRANSPORT_WRAP` and
  `HERMES_SKIP_ASYNC_WRAP` flags, `api_key = 'external-process'`, and the check in
  `create()` that returns a coroutine only when the direct caller is a coroutine inside a
  running event loop).

